	"data": "Journal Archaeology — 2026-08-21\n\nTwo journals, eight years apart. The same person at 20 and 25. What survives? What changes? What does the distance reveal?\n\nThe 2018 Journal — Chris at 20\n\nHe's five days into a jogging habit. Just got a job as a cashier at Home Depot. He's describing his dream workspace — a place with computers, a blacksmith forge outside, a sensory deprivation tank, a VR clubhouse. He wants to build things and test them. He says \"I'm free. I can go in whatever direction I…",
